1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,202
That's not CGI.

2
00:00:02,702 --> 00:00:04,536
That's thousands of drones

3
00:00:05,036 --> 00:00:06,545
over the river in Chongqing

4
00:00:07,045 --> 00:00:09,304
and the whole city came out to watch.

5
00:00:09,854 --> 00:00:11,906
I spent six days here.

6
00:00:12,353 --> 00:00:13,462
but not as a tourist

7
00:00:13,962 --> 00:00:16,237
I came on a study mission from Singapore.

8
00:00:16,737 --> 00:00:20,756
government briefings, hospitals, robot labs.

9
00:00:21,134 --> 00:00:24,098
doors tourists don't get to walk through.

10
00:00:24,648 --> 00:00:26,833
So this video does two things.

11
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:31,205
It answers every question you'll have before you visit.

12
00:00:31,705 --> 00:00:34,318
and it shows you what's behind those doors.

13
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:38,568
I'm Shawn, I'm Singaporean, and this is Shawn in China.

14
00:00:38,887 --> 00:00:39,884
Let's go.

15
00:00:40,434 --> 00:00:42,716
First question everyone asked me

16
00:00:43,216 --> 00:00:44,346
Do you need a visa?

17
00:00:44,846 --> 00:00:46,796
if you're Singaporean,

18
00:00:47,296 --> 00:00:49,384
Since February 2024,

19
00:00:49,666 --> 00:00:51,218
Singapore and China

20
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:56,448
Let each other's citizens visit visa-free for up to 30 days.

21
00:00:56,998 --> 00:01:00,472
check the 240 hour visa free transit.

22
00:01:00,972 --> 00:01:04,745
Chongqing's airport is one of the eligible entry points.

23
00:01:05,245 --> 00:01:09,658
as long as you're flying onto a third country, the rules change.

24
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:12,462
So check the official list before you book.

25
00:01:13,012 --> 00:01:15,341
Second question, how do you pay?

26
00:01:15,841 --> 00:01:16,753
Here's the thing.

27
00:01:17,253 --> 00:01:20,871
China barely uses cash or cards in shops.

28
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:23,875
It runs on Alipay and WeChat Pay.

29
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:27,680
And both now accept foreign visa and mastercard.

30
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:31,014
Set them up and verify them before you fly.

31
00:01:31,514 --> 00:01:34,161
I used Alipay and WeChat Pay.

32
00:01:34,661 --> 00:01:36,454
And it worked almost everywhere.

33
00:01:36,954 --> 00:01:39,214
still carry a bit of cash for backup.

34
00:01:39,764 --> 00:01:40,210
third

35
00:01:40,686 --> 00:01:44,869
Google, WhatsApp, and Instagram don't work on Chinese networks.

36
00:01:45,369 --> 00:01:48,710
Download offline maps and a translation app before you land.

37
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:51,327
Then we had a welcome dinner

38
00:01:51,827 --> 00:01:56,911
round table, lazy Susan, and a dish every 30 seconds.

39
00:01:57,397 --> 00:01:59,754
I didn't know half of what I was eating.

40
00:02:00,109 --> 00:02:01,395
I finished all of it.

41
00:02:01,945 --> 00:02:03,089
Quick context

42
00:02:03,589 --> 00:02:06,220
Because Chongqing confuses everyone.

43
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:09,606
Why do people call it the 8D city?

44
00:02:10,156 --> 00:02:12,882
It's built on mountains where two rivers

45
00:02:13,382 --> 00:02:15,260
The Yangtze and the

46
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,966
There's barely any flat ground.

47
00:02:18,307 --> 00:02:20,265
So the city stacks on itself.

48
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:22,416
Roads run over roofs.

49
00:02:22,916 --> 00:02:26,879
you walk into a mall on the ground floor and walk out on the 8th

50
00:02:27,379 --> 00:02:30,622
Your map app has no idea which level you're on

51
00:02:31,172 --> 00:02:36,739
We started at the planning exhibition gallery, which is basically the city explaining itself.

52
00:02:37,239 --> 00:02:39,739
The whole municipality has around

53
00:02:40,239 --> 00:02:41,850
32 million people,

54
00:02:42,295 --> 00:02:44,201
and it's about the size of Austria.

55
00:02:44,701 --> 00:02:48,886
Most of that is countryside, but the core still feels endless.

56
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:52,605
Then a briefing I didn't expect to find so interesting:

57
00:02:53,093 --> 00:02:56,683
the China–Singapore Chongqing Connectivity Initiative.

58
00:02:57,183 --> 00:02:59,054
It's a government-to-government project.

59
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:03,738
Singapore's third in China, after Suzhou and Tianjin.

60
00:03:04,238 --> 00:03:08,120
Finance, logistics, aviation, digital links.

61
00:03:08,570 --> 00:03:13,121
It's why a Singaporean study group gets a seat at these tables at all.

62
00:03:13,671 --> 00:03:17,146
Even the hospital we visited that afternoon was Singaporean:

63
00:03:17,646 --> 00:03:20,512
Raffles Hospital in the middle of Chongqing.

64
00:03:21,062 --> 00:03:21,661
And at night,

65
00:03:21,979 --> 00:03:22,798
Guanyinqiao.

66
00:03:23,298 --> 00:03:25,214
screens on every building

67
00:03:25,595 --> 00:03:27,895
and the whole street out walking.

68
00:03:28,445 --> 00:03:31,273
Day three. Our group split in two.

69
00:03:31,773 --> 00:03:34,986
Architects went to see urban renewal projects.

70
00:03:35,486 --> 00:03:37,883
I went the healthcare-and-tech route.

71
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:39,205
First stop:

72
00:03:39,705 --> 00:03:40,698
Liangjiang

73
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,623
Life Science City.

74
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:49,168
picture a whole district planned around medical devices, biotech, and digital health.

75
00:03:49,668 --> 00:03:51,197
That's what this is.

76
00:03:51,747 --> 00:03:54,036
Then, Haifu Medical.

77
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:55,114
They build

78
00:03:55,488 --> 00:03:58,186
HIFU machines:

79
00:03:58,686 --> 00:04:05,019
focused ultrasound that treats tumors without a single cut, developed here in Chongqing.

80
00:04:05,569 --> 00:04:09,201
And then the afternoon everyone back home asked about

81
00:04:09,701 --> 00:04:12,434
Are robots really everywhere in China?

82
00:04:19,984 --> 00:04:22,334
This humanoid danced for us.

83
00:04:22,834 --> 00:04:25,114
A robot dog trotted around the hall.

84
00:04:25,614 --> 00:04:27,714
What got me wasn't the tricks.

85
00:04:28,102 --> 00:04:31,414
it was how normal it was to the people showing us.

86
00:04:31,914 --> 00:04:33,395
To them this is a product line,

87
00:04:33,766 --> 00:04:34,671
not a demo.

88
00:04:35,221 --> 00:04:36,759
Dinner.

89
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:40,542
Honest answer to "how spicy is Chongqing hotpot?"

90
00:04:41,042 --> 00:04:42,258
Very spicy.

91
00:04:42,758 --> 00:04:43,802
It's mala,

92
00:04:44,163 --> 00:04:48,642
So the chili burns and the Sichuan pepper numbs your mouth at the same time.

93
00:04:49,142 --> 00:04:52,011
So my tip is to order a yuanyang pot,

94
00:04:52,511 --> 00:04:55,686
split down the middle, with a mild broth on one side.

95
00:04:56,186 --> 00:04:57,475
Nobody judges you.

96
00:04:57,975 --> 00:04:58,811
Maybe a little.

97
00:04:59,361 --> 00:05:01,957
If you think Chongqing is only neon,

98
00:05:02,409 --> 00:05:03,635
start here.

99
00:05:04,135 --> 00:05:09,897
Eling No. 2 Factory used to print money for China's central bank in the 1940s.

100
00:05:10,397 --> 00:05:13,712
Now it's murals, cafés and studios.

101
00:05:14,212 --> 00:05:17,873
And yes, that's a PlayStation controller on a wall.

102
00:05:18,423 --> 00:05:22,325
in the afternoon, the connectivity initiative exhibition hall.

103
00:05:22,825 --> 00:05:26,772
Seeing Singapore's leaders on the wall in Chongqing hit differently.

104
00:05:27,272 --> 00:05:29,121
Then a trade conference.

105
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:32,837
Singapore and Chongqing businesses trying to find each other.

106
00:05:33,387 --> 00:05:35,459
And then the night everyone comes for.

107
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:36,875
Hongyadong.

108
00:05:41,425 --> 00:05:44,393
It's a cliffside complex of stilt houses.

109
00:05:44,738 --> 00:05:46,095
lit gold,

110
00:05:46,595 --> 00:05:49,367
and people say it looks like Spirited Away.

111
00:05:49,867 --> 00:05:50,778
When should you go?

112
00:05:51,278 --> 00:05:51,993
After dark.

113
00:05:52,493 --> 00:05:57,350
The usual advice is to skip the 7:30 crush and aim for after eight.

114
00:05:57,850 --> 00:05:59,142
Busy, but happy.

115
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:00,737
Is it safe at night?

116
00:06:01,237 --> 00:06:03,062
From everything I saw, yes.

117
00:06:03,562 --> 00:06:04,899
Families out late,

118
00:06:05,274 --> 00:06:06,456
people everywhere.

119
00:06:06,956 --> 00:06:09,497
Just mind your phone in the crowds like anywhere.

120
00:06:10,047 --> 00:06:12,300
And stand on the river side and look back.

121
00:06:12,584 --> 00:06:15,289
That's the 8D city in one view.

122
00:06:15,839 --> 00:06:18,335
Day five was the nerdy day.

123
00:06:18,835 --> 00:06:20,725
And I meant that as a compliment.

124
00:06:21,275 --> 00:06:23,728
Ever heard of East data West computing?

125
00:06:24,228 --> 00:06:27,372
China's richest cities are on the East Coast.

126
00:06:27,731 --> 00:06:30,171
And so is most of the demand for computing.

127
00:06:30,623 --> 00:06:33,243
But land and power are cheaper out west.

128
00:06:33,743 --> 00:06:40,766
So the country is building huge data centres in places like Chongqing to do computing for the east.

129
00:06:41,266 --> 00:06:44,115
No filming inside, so here's the group photo.

130
00:06:44,665 --> 00:06:47,069
The other theme that week was aging.

131
00:06:47,569 --> 00:06:51,279
China has more than 300 million people over 60.

132
00:06:51,779 --> 00:06:58,331
Across the trip, we saw how companies here use AI and digital tools for elder care and health.

133
00:06:58,831 --> 00:07:02,164
Singapore is aging too. So I took a lot of notes.

134
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:03,445
Then, food.

135
00:07:03,945 --> 00:07:05,589
What should I eat besides hot pot?

136
00:07:06,089 --> 00:07:07,446
Jiefangbei Food Street.

137
00:07:07,946 --> 00:07:11,929
skewers, Chongqing noodles, snacks I couldn't name.

138
00:07:12,418 --> 00:07:14,237
If there's a queue, join it.

139
00:07:19,787 --> 00:07:20,835
Is it expensive?

140
00:07:21,335 --> 00:07:22,988
Not compared with Singapore

141
00:07:23,538 --> 00:07:26,115
Last morning: a reflection session,

142
00:07:26,609 --> 00:07:29,590
where we shared what we'd take back to Singapore.

143
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:34,381
Then I had one afternoon for myself and I did all the tourist things.

144
00:07:34,931 --> 00:07:37,140
Getting around is easier than it looks.

145
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:41,940
The metro and monorail are cheap, and yes, at Liziba,

146
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:45,812
The train really does go through a residential building.

147
00:07:46,312 --> 00:07:49,139
Wear good shoes because there are stairs everywhere.

148
00:07:49,689 --> 00:07:55,551
I took the cableway over the Yangtze, which has carried commuters since the 1980s.

149
00:07:56,051 --> 00:07:59,428
An uncle was writing characters on the pavement with water.

150
00:07:59,928 --> 00:08:02,765
A phone shop let me play with folding phones.

151
00:08:03,236 --> 00:08:08,545
And there's hotpot inside an old air-raid shelter. Because, of course, there is.

152
00:08:09,095 --> 00:08:12,878
So is a study trip worth it compared with traveling on your own?

153
00:08:13,428 --> 00:08:14,170
Definitely.

154
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:16,443
You get rooms you can't book.

155
00:08:16,943 --> 00:08:21,401
and you come home with a group chat full of people who are in the room with you.

156
00:08:21,951 --> 00:08:26,249
The programme I went on is Ngee Ann Polytechnic's Travel & Learn to Chongqing.

157
00:08:26,749 --> 00:08:29,872
If you're Singaporean, it's SkillsFuture-supported,

158
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:31,886
accommodation's included.

159
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:34,955
Check the next intake through the link below.

160
00:08:35,505 --> 00:08:36,492
When should you go?

161
00:08:36,992 --> 00:08:38,549
Spring or autumn

162
00:08:39,049 --> 00:08:40,219
Summer is very hot.

163
00:08:40,585 --> 00:08:42,035
I went in mid-October.

164
00:08:42,585 --> 00:08:45,396
Got a question about Chongqing I didn't answer?

165
00:08:45,896 --> 00:08:47,125
Leave it in the comments.

166
00:08:47,526 --> 00:08:49,833
I'll answer the best ones in the next video.

167
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:51,154
I'm Shawn,

168
00:08:51,654 --> 00:08:52,994
this is Shawn in China,

169
00:08:53,389 --> 00:08:55,577
and I'll see you in the next city.

